From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akram-composio <akram@composio.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:26:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] web: remove upstream promotion, support links and update nags

Why: Kimono Photos is part of a household platform that Kimono updates and
supports. Purchase/licence prompts, "new version" announcements and links to
immich.app, GitHub or Discord are noise or point people at the wrong place.

What must survive upstream changes:
- Sidebar bottom shows storage only: no PurchaseInfo (buy/supporter) and no
  ServerStatus (version + "new version available" link to GitHub).
- User settings have no Purchase section.
- Account panel has no "Support & feedback" button (HelpAndFeedbackModal with
  docs/GitHub/Discord links is unreachable).
- No VersionAnnouncement modal on release events (root +layout.svelte).
- No "My Immich link" command (copies a my.immich.app URL) in the palette.
- Error page has no Discord / changelog / docker-help links.
- Admin, onboarding, maintenance and duplicates copy keeps its wording but no
  longer links to docs.immich.app (the <Link> is replaced by the bare message).
- Routes such as /buy and /link stay (nothing links to them) to keep the diff small.

